{"cluster_id": "C-3063", "topic": "Dead-precommit removal moved from GC to", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B012-053"], "canonical_claim": "Dead-precommit removal moved from GC to the writer, which appends exact `owner_transition` removals; GC reclaims the resulting blobs through ordinary edge cancellation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-refsnaplog-coverage-audit.md#L56-L70"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3064", "topic": "Pool-member decommission performs full srid erasure", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B014-052"], "canonical_claim": "Pool-member decommission performs full srid erasure of namespaces, manifest debris, staging, roots objects, and the slot, while subsequent normal GC rounds reclaim the now-unreferenced blob bytes.", "issue_ids": ["B200"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-pool-member-decommission-design.md#decisions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3065", "topic": "On atomic-write storages, VersionMetadataOnDisk writes version", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-019", "B015-085", "B051-076"], "canonical_claim": "On atomic-write storages, `VersionMetadataOnDisk` writes version information with one `writeFile` instead of a temporary file plus rename.; When `supportsAtomicFileWrites` is true, `VersionMetadataOnDisk` writes `txn_version.txt` directly instead of using a temporary file and `replaceFile`, because the storage itself provides atomic publication. Additionally, Since Task 5's `supportsAtomicFileWrites` capability, `VersionMetadataOnDisk::storeInfoToDataPartStorage` writes `txn_version.txt` as a single atomic `writeFile` with no `.tmp` file and no `replaceFile` call; `ContentAddressedTransaction::moveFile`'s legacy mutable-per-part-file destination routing is dead code in production for CA, still present pending a later mechanical sweep but unreached by any current write path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L561-L573", "docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#version-metadata-on-disk-cpp", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#mvcc-short-circuit-and-the-eager-hook-deletion"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3066", "topic": "The freeze metadata_version_written_by_freeze special case is", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B016-018"], "canonical_claim": "The freeze `metadata_version_written_by_freeze` special case is removed because an identical post-clone rewrite is absorbed by the byte-equal repoint no-op, while a differing rewrite may legally repoint.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#task-10"]}
